# A standard library generic enum instantiated in two units that never see each other: `result<string,
# int32>` is built and read inside `modresult`'s own unit and instantiated again here. The payload is a
# `string`, a named type lowered per unit, which is the shape `lib_optpayload` was written to reproduce.
#
# It is also the only coverage of a stdlib **static** across a module boundary - a case constructor is a
# static on a generic owner, and nothing else in `stdlib/` declares one.
modules: modules/lib_resultuser
flags: --track-allocations

--- OUT --->
from the library
the library refused
1
from the library
-2
mine
from the library
